WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.209 --> 00:00:01.919
[Annie] <i>Previously on</i> Sterling Point…

2
00:00:02.503 --> 00:00:06.173
[Annie] <i>I drank way too much.</i>
<i>then I went home with Rory.</i>

3
00:00:06.257 --> 00:00:08.259
-You had sex with Rory?
-[shushes]

4
00:00:08.342 --> 00:00:09.385
-Annie?
-[Annie] Dad.

5
00:00:09.468 --> 00:00:10.970
-What?
-What are you doing here?

6
00:00:11.053 --> 00:00:13.931
[Annie] <i>And now I'm like.</i>
<i>does this mess up the Ellis thing?</i>

7
00:00:14.014 --> 00:00:16.392
Ellis. sometimes
I can't tell if you hate me.

8
00:00:16.475 --> 00:00:19.395
I actually can't even think of one thing
I don't like about you.

9
00:00:22.106 --> 00:00:23.566
You're so beautiful.

10
00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:26.652
[Annie] I didn't really. like.
experience my childhood.

11
00:00:26.736 --> 00:00:28.779
Annie. you don't need to be fixed. though.

12
00:00:28.904 --> 00:00:30.114
[Annie] <i>What happened. Dad?</i>

13
00:00:30.197 --> 00:00:32.491
Your mom didn't wanna
live in New York anymore.

14
00:00:32.575 --> 00:00:35.703
She filed for divorce and refused
to bring you guys back home.

15
00:00:36.287 --> 00:00:40.666
It sounds to me
like she was unhappy in her life.

16
00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:43.502
and so she came here
to try to make things better.

17
00:00:43.586 --> 00:00:46.547
and I don't understand
why that's an insane thing to do.

18
00:00:46.630 --> 00:00:48.549
'Cause she came up here and lost her mind!

19
00:00:48.632 --> 00:00:51.594
You know what happened to Goldie.
and it sure as hell wasn't me.

20
00:00:51.677 --> 00:00:53.387
It was the biggest mistake of her life.

21
00:00:53.471 --> 00:00:55.431
I know she didn't love you anymore.

22
00:00:56.307 --> 00:00:57.600
[grunts]

23
00:00:57.683 --> 00:00:59.769
-Fuck!
-[Kate] <i>Were you in love with her?</i>

24
00:01:00.394 --> 00:01:01.854
Is Ramona yours?

25
00:01:03.272 --> 00:01:05.566
Joe is your dad. Ramona.

26
00:01:06.066 --> 00:01:06.942
You two knew?

27
00:01:08.110 --> 00:01:10.613
You said. "No more secrets."

28
00:01:10.696 --> 00:01:12.406
-No--
-Ramona. Hey. Ramona. wait.

29
00:01:12.490 --> 00:01:13.824
[Sully] Ramona.

30
00:01:14.784 --> 00:01:15.951
Wait!

31
00:01:16.535 --> 00:01:17.536
Ramona!

32
00:01:24.376 --> 00:01:27.379
["Ain't Quite Right" playing]

33
00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:35.074
Support us and become VIP member 
to remove all ads from www.OpenSubtitles.org

34
00:02:02.289 --> 00:02:03.457
Ramona!

35
00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:06.126
Ramona!

36
00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:09.880
Ramona! Girl. where are you?

37
00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:14.134
[Annie] Ramona!

38
00:02:14.218 --> 00:02:15.219
[Ellis] Ramona!

39
00:02:16.887 --> 00:02:18.556
[Annie] Where else could she go?

40
00:02:18.639 --> 00:02:20.266
She could be anywhere. honestly.

41
00:02:21.934 --> 00:02:24.311
I've actually never felt like
a more terrible person.

42
00:02:24.895 --> 00:02:26.397
I feel like I ruined her life.

43
00:02:27.773 --> 00:02:30.109
No. Annie. no. This isn't your fault.

44
00:02:30.943 --> 00:02:32.236
This is on our dads.

45
00:02:33.487 --> 00:02:35.489
They're the ones
who should feel like shit.

46
00:02:38.075 --> 00:02:39.618
[exhales]

47
00:02:39.702 --> 00:02:41.412
She couldn't have gone that far. right?

48
00:02:42.371 --> 00:02:44.373
I feel like she wouldn't do that to Oona.

49
00:02:47.501 --> 00:02:49.837
I don't think she'd do it
to her sister either.

50
00:02:51.171 --> 00:02:52.006
We'll find her.

51
00:02:56.886 --> 00:02:57.761
Ramona!

52
00:02:58.345 --> 00:02:59.305
Ramona!

53
00:03:07.771 --> 00:03:10.441
[Denise] Tell me about
this philosopher who lived in a barrel.

54
00:03:10.524 --> 00:03:14.320
-Yeah. his name is Diogenes. And he--
-Who?

55
00:03:14.403 --> 00:03:18.449
-How you know all this shit?
-He'd pee in the street and stuff. It was…

56
00:03:18.532 --> 00:03:20.868
-[chuckles]
-Oh. hi.

57
00:03:20.951 --> 00:03:22.953
-[Denise] Anything?
-No.

58
00:03:23.037 --> 00:03:24.371
[Denise] Any news?

59
00:03:24.455 --> 00:03:26.248
What about Joe? Where is he?

60
00:03:26.749 --> 00:03:30.127
Uh. I think he's also
out there looking for her.

61
00:03:30.878 --> 00:03:32.338
Good. As he should be.

62
00:03:36.884 --> 00:03:38.552
Do you think she's fucking with us?

63
00:03:38.636 --> 00:03:40.679
Ramona? Absolutely. She's fine.

64
00:03:40.763 --> 00:03:43.140
I ran away. like. a hundred times
when I was a youth.

65
00:03:43.974 --> 00:03:45.225
Mom. what is wrong with you?

66
00:03:45.309 --> 00:03:46.602
What?

67
00:03:46.685 --> 00:03:49.229
You're fully responsible
for a missing 17-year-old.

68
00:03:49.313 --> 00:03:50.898
How am I fully responsible. honey?

69
00:03:50.981 --> 00:03:54.026
Ramona needed the truth and I was
the only one willing to say anything.

70
00:03:54.109 --> 00:03:57.029
-But that's inappropriate.
-Like. honestly. I mean. you kinda ate.

71
00:03:57.947 --> 00:04:00.658
Wild move. and I respect it.

72
00:04:00.741 --> 00:04:04.954
Thanks. Connor. See? Not everybody thinks
that I'm the worst person in the world.

73
00:04:05.037 --> 00:04:07.665
-She's your sister. Connor.
-Yeah. And I love my gay sister.

74
00:04:08.666 --> 00:04:10.167
Tell Steven I'm in the boathouse.

75
00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:11.752
Okay. sweetie.

76
00:04:13.003 --> 00:04:14.922
He just weaned off his Wellbutrin.

77
00:04:15.005 --> 00:04:17.174
and I think he needs that
on top of the Lexapro.

78
00:04:17.800 --> 00:04:19.802
That is a successful combo.

79
00:04:19.885 --> 00:04:20.970
Right?

80
00:04:26.475 --> 00:04:28.435
-It's not about you.
-Yeah. I know that.

81
00:04:31.271 --> 00:04:32.898
-Okay. let it out.
-No. I hate crying.

82
00:04:32.982 --> 00:04:35.859
I don't like it when you bottle things up.
Just come here. please.

83
00:04:35.943 --> 00:04:38.904
Just… I got you. baby.

84
00:04:38.988 --> 00:04:41.865
[Oona crying] Just. like. is she gone?

85
00:04:41.949 --> 00:04:43.826
'Cause she literally disappeared
for a year.

86
00:04:44.493 --> 00:04:46.912
[Sully] Let's think this through.
She took the tinner.

87
00:04:46.996 --> 00:04:50.290
she can't be found on the lakes.
and she clearly wants to be far away

88
00:04:50.374 --> 00:04:53.502
from everyone here.
which I totally understand.

89
00:04:54.003 --> 00:04:56.880
Did you check to see if Gordon's car
is still parked in town?

90
00:04:56.964 --> 00:04:58.632
[Oona] Oh. my God. [sniffles]

91
00:05:00.342 --> 00:05:01.468
I forgot she had his car.

92
00:05:01.552 --> 00:05:03.387
-Girl…
-Right. Yeah. okay.

93
00:05:03.470 --> 00:05:05.806
She obviously took it.
But where would she go?

94
00:05:05.889 --> 00:05:08.142
She probably went home to Barrie.

95
00:05:09.143 --> 00:05:11.895
Oh. my God. You are a literal genius.

96
00:05:13.147 --> 00:05:15.441
-Thank you. Yeah.
-It's just common sense.

97
00:05:15.524 --> 00:05:18.610
Is there any chance that your mums
would let us take the food truck?

98
00:05:18.694 --> 00:05:20.487
-Not in this lifetime. babes.
-Why?

99
00:05:20.571 --> 00:05:22.448
-You've totaled three cars.
-No. it was one.

100
00:05:22.531 --> 00:05:25.325
It was three. It was three.
I was there. and it was three.

101
00:05:25.409 --> 00:05:28.412
But I do know somebody
who does have a car.

102
00:05:39.089 --> 00:05:40.507
Ta-da.

103
00:05:46.096 --> 00:05:47.139
Take your pick.

104
00:05:49.183 --> 00:05:50.726
Yeah. She'll do.

105
00:05:51.310 --> 00:05:52.853
Yeah. Okay. Perfect.

106
00:05:52.936 --> 00:05:54.563
That's… That's my dad's favorite.

107
00:05:54.646 --> 00:05:55.481
Thank you.

108
00:05:56.815 --> 00:06:01.570
Um. and then just to review.
so the "R" stands for…

109
00:06:01.653 --> 00:06:04.823
-"Reverse."
-"Reverse." I knew that. Okay. great.

110
00:06:05.407 --> 00:06:07.951
And the "D"? The "D"…

111
00:06:08.619 --> 00:06:10.704
-Oona. "drive."
-Amazing.

112
00:06:11.705 --> 00:06:13.624
Amazing. You did it. You passed the test.

113
00:06:13.707 --> 00:06:15.417
That's it. Ah. well done.

114
00:06:16.085 --> 00:06:18.212
Do you even know what to do
at a red light?

115
00:06:18.962 --> 00:06:20.380
You ask her out to dinner.

116
00:06:22.007 --> 00:06:24.927
What is this. with the left-hand
steering wheel thing?

117
00:06:27.137 --> 00:06:33.393
Okay. the total comes to $175 even.
Will that be cash or charge today?

118
00:06:33.477 --> 00:06:35.938
Last time I was here.
your son said you were cash only.

119
00:06:36.522 --> 00:06:38.482
[customer 2] Dude. that was
annoying as hell.

120
00:06:38.565 --> 00:06:40.317
We had to drive 30 minutes

121
00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:42.069
for some machine to spit out cash.

122
00:06:45.531 --> 00:06:50.410
Uh. sorry. [hesitating] System must've
been down. I apologize for that.

123
00:06:50.494 --> 00:06:51.662
You should look into that.

124
00:06:51.745 --> 00:06:52.579
Here you go.

125
00:06:54.164 --> 00:06:54.998
And these.

126
00:06:56.542 --> 00:06:57.376
Please.

127
00:07:08.345 --> 00:07:09.638
[Joe] Any word from her?

128
00:07:09.721 --> 00:07:12.558
No. I'm heading back out with Annie.

129
00:07:16.061 --> 00:07:17.688
[Joe] Your mom found the tape.

130
00:07:22.901 --> 00:07:23.777
[sighs]

131
00:07:25.487 --> 00:07:27.614
I left it for you.
I didn't think she'd find it.

132
00:07:27.698 --> 00:07:30.367
Yeah. well. she did.

133
00:07:33.787 --> 00:07:34.997
And I found the money.

134
00:07:37.249 --> 00:07:40.794
[sighing] $7.345. Ellis?

135
00:07:42.462 --> 00:07:44.464
Where the hell did this come from? What…

136
00:07:45.591 --> 00:07:47.843
Are you dealing or something? What…

137
00:07:47.926 --> 00:07:50.512
You think I'm dealing drugs? Wow.

138
00:07:50.596 --> 00:07:52.848
You are so checked out.
it's actually insane.

139
00:07:52.931 --> 00:07:56.268
-Don't avoid the question.
-From the man who hid something so massive

140
00:07:56.351 --> 00:07:58.770
from everyone our whole lives?
What do you mean?

141
00:07:58.854 --> 00:08:00.856
Look. I fucked up.
You think I don't know that?

142
00:08:01.773 --> 00:08:04.860
I am trying to make sure that you don't.

143
00:08:08.447 --> 00:08:09.364
[sighs]

144
00:08:12.451 --> 00:08:14.661
I've been…
I've been overcharging people.

145
00:08:14.745 --> 00:08:17.789
-What?
-Yeah. just $50 here and there. So what?

146
00:08:18.832 --> 00:08:19.791
Why would you do that?

147
00:08:19.875 --> 00:08:21.543
Because you're stupid not to.

148
00:08:21.627 --> 00:08:24.671
-Ellis. watch it.
-50 bucks is nothing to these rich people.

149
00:08:24.755 --> 00:08:27.424
Fifty bucks over and over is
everything to us.

150
00:08:27.507 --> 00:08:28.425
-We're fine.
-No!

151
00:08:28.508 --> 00:08:29.801
No. we're not!

152
00:08:29.885 --> 00:08:33.680
Mom works nights and holidays
'cause the marina's barely scraping by.

153
00:08:33.764 --> 00:08:36.683
and you won't raise the prices
and run the business as you should.

154
00:08:36.767 --> 00:08:39.519
-Yeah. what's the money for?
-For a fuckin' safety net.

155
00:08:40.854 --> 00:08:42.147
We need six more tinners.

156
00:08:42.231 --> 00:08:45.108
-We need to fix the roof.
-We're gonna get all those things. Ellis.

157
00:08:45.192 --> 00:08:47.319
-We're fine.
-You're in denial. Dad.

158
00:08:47.402 --> 00:08:51.281
And. apparently.
you have been my whole life.

159
00:08:53.700 --> 00:08:56.662
-You're her dad.
-I'm sorry. I…

160
00:08:56.745 --> 00:08:57.663
I…

161
00:08:58.455 --> 00:09:01.416
-I never wanted it to come out like this.
-What was your plan. then?

162
00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:03.001
Did you even have one?

163
00:09:03.585 --> 00:09:04.753
-I don't…
-See?

164
00:09:06.255 --> 00:09:07.506
This is exactly what I mean.

165
00:09:10.300 --> 00:09:11.301
Ellis. just…

166
00:09:41.456 --> 00:09:42.291
Okay.

167
00:09:52.301 --> 00:09:53.593
[knocking at door]

168
00:09:58.932 --> 00:10:00.100
[sighing]

169
00:10:00.183 --> 00:10:03.729
If I wasn't so happy to see you.
I would be so furious right now.

170
00:10:12.738 --> 00:10:14.114
Please don't do that again.

171
00:10:17.242 --> 00:10:18.076
Okay.

172
00:10:24.916 --> 00:10:28.295
Sorry. I know it's. like. very depressing.

173
00:10:28.837 --> 00:10:32.299
No. Hey. do not apologize for that. okay?

174
00:10:32.382 --> 00:10:33.383
Yeah.

175
00:10:34.426 --> 00:10:37.262
I mean. if you're gonna apologize.
you should apologize for just--

176
00:10:37.346 --> 00:10:40.057
For what? Being born in the first place?

177
00:10:40.849 --> 00:10:41.683
No.

178
00:10:41.767 --> 00:10:42.809
No.

179
00:10:44.436 --> 00:10:45.395
Hey. don't do that.

180
00:10:46.480 --> 00:10:50.067
Look. you can do that with everyone else
for the rest of your life if you want.

181
00:10:51.109 --> 00:10:55.822
You can disappear. you can go dark.
go quiet. take space.

182
00:10:55.906 --> 00:10:58.617
None of that is off limits.
and there is no judgment.

183
00:11:00.660 --> 00:11:02.454
But you can't bail on me. okay?

184
00:11:05.540 --> 00:11:08.919
Tell me what you're feeling right now
in this second.

185
00:11:16.176 --> 00:11:17.135
I feel like this…

186
00:11:19.262 --> 00:11:21.765
leftover problem
everyone has to deal with.

187
00:11:28.730 --> 00:11:30.190
God. I hate being back here.

188
00:11:32.275 --> 00:11:33.902
It's just all so dark

189
00:11:35.612 --> 00:11:38.323
and… scary.

190
00:11:38.407 --> 00:11:40.617
How are you not scared of it?

191
00:11:42.369 --> 00:11:43.620
Or me?

192
00:11:50.502 --> 00:11:51.795
Because I love you.

193
00:11:53.463 --> 00:11:55.465
["Wishes" playing]

194
00:11:56.883 --> 00:11:58.009
I do.

195
00:11:59.594 --> 00:12:01.847
I really. really love you.

196
00:12:15.735 --> 00:12:16.862
I love you too.

197
00:12:26.538 --> 00:12:27.706
Can we please go home now?

198
00:12:27.789 --> 00:12:30.041
[chuckles] Yeah.

199
00:12:47.392 --> 00:12:48.310
Annie?

200
00:12:51.521 --> 00:12:52.481
Hello?

201
00:12:54.107 --> 00:12:56.026
[whispering] Ellis. Hey.

202
00:13:06.745 --> 00:13:07.704
I like this.

203
00:13:08.371 --> 00:13:11.291
[Annie] See? What did I tell you?
They always calm me down.

204
00:13:12.209 --> 00:13:13.960
-Closets.
-Right?

205
00:13:15.879 --> 00:13:19.090
Thank God something's working. 'cause
my next resort was a thunder jacket.

206
00:13:20.592 --> 00:13:22.219
[chuckles] I'm sorry. A what?

207
00:13:22.302 --> 00:13:24.638
-Do you not know what that is?
-A thunder jacket?

208
00:13:24.721 --> 00:13:25.555
It's like a…

209
00:13:26.181 --> 00:13:28.016
It's like a jacket for anxious dogs.

210
00:13:28.517 --> 00:13:31.061
It's supposed to feel like
a really tight hug.

211
00:13:31.144 --> 00:13:32.812
-Oh. Right.
-Yeah.

212
00:13:34.481 --> 00:13:35.690
Sounds kind of nice. no?

213
00:13:36.816 --> 00:13:37.859
Yeah.

214
00:13:39.611 --> 00:13:40.570
Does it work?

215
00:13:41.446 --> 00:13:43.740
Apparently. We'll see when I get one.

216
00:13:50.705 --> 00:13:51.623
Well. come here then.

217
00:14:03.343 --> 00:14:06.346
["Rowing Song" playing]

218
00:14:47.887 --> 00:14:49.764
[softly] Why are you so good at this?

219
00:14:53.935 --> 00:14:56.563
[softly] I don't really know
how to answer that.

220
00:14:56.646 --> 00:14:58.064
It's okay. Just do it again.

221
00:15:32.057 --> 00:15:35.060
Steven. we're alone.

222
00:15:35.143 --> 00:15:36.645
[Steven clears throat]

223
00:15:36.728 --> 00:15:39.439
We are on an island
in the middle of nowhere. Canada.

224
00:15:41.858 --> 00:15:45.403
If you need to get something
off your chest. you should.

225
00:15:46.988 --> 00:15:48.782
'cause I know you're not okay right now.

226
00:15:49.282 --> 00:15:50.617
What makes you think that?

227
00:15:55.580 --> 00:15:56.915
Do you think I'm the bad guy?

228
00:15:58.541 --> 00:15:59.793
I don't think it matters.

229
00:16:01.920 --> 00:16:05.340
Well. here I am again.
fighting for my family.

230
00:16:05.423 --> 00:16:07.550
Trying to bring my kids home. Again.

231
00:16:07.634 --> 00:16:10.595
Annie hates my guts.
just like her mother did.

232
00:16:11.429 --> 00:16:13.598
So. I don't know. I think it might.

233
00:16:14.849 --> 00:16:18.353
Annie was always a well-behaved kid.
but she was angry.

234
00:16:18.436 --> 00:16:19.646
mostly at me.

235
00:16:20.855 --> 00:16:25.026
And I thought. when she grows up.
she'll figure out I'm not the bad guy.

236
00:16:25.110 --> 00:16:27.278
I didn't take her mom away. I didn't…

237
00:16:28.571 --> 00:16:29.739
wreck this family.

238
00:16:32.409 --> 00:16:35.620
In kindergarten. she had to draw
this portrait of our family.

239
00:16:35.704 --> 00:16:40.125
so she drew the three of us.
Connor. herself. and me. at the park.

240
00:16:41.668 --> 00:16:43.545
I'm pushing Connor on a swing.

241
00:16:43.628 --> 00:16:46.589
but she's over there by herself. alone.

242
00:16:47.882 --> 00:16:50.051
She said she was lookin' for somethin'.

243
00:16:51.970 --> 00:16:55.849
I mean. even in kindergarten.
she could feel what she'd lost. you know?

244
00:16:55.932 --> 00:16:59.728
Her mom. her birth family. her sister.

245
00:17:00.687 --> 00:17:03.231
Any chance at a normal childhood.

246
00:17:04.107 --> 00:17:04.941
She knew.

247
00:17:06.860 --> 00:17:10.447
Honey. it was a powder keg.
It was always gonna blow.

248
00:17:12.157 --> 00:17:16.619
But everybody survived. and now you can
just put the pieces back together.

249
00:17:16.703 --> 00:17:18.496
-I don't know if that'll happen.
-Hey.

250
00:17:21.374 --> 00:17:23.084
Honey. you did the best you could.

251
00:17:24.294 --> 00:17:27.297
But does it even matter?

252
00:17:30.633 --> 00:17:31.843
[sighs]

253
00:17:35.096 --> 00:17:36.556
That's all you left me?

254
00:17:39.726 --> 00:17:42.729
["Hey There Cowgirl" playing]

255
00:18:06.377 --> 00:18:07.921
Oh. okay. Ow! Ow!

256
00:18:08.004 --> 00:18:10.381
Okay. don't take it out on me.
Mommy. please?

257
00:18:10.465 --> 00:18:12.634
Connor. do you think
she really likes Ellis?

258
00:18:12.717 --> 00:18:14.928
I don't know.
Her only other boyfriend was gay.

259
00:18:15.011 --> 00:18:16.387
-Right.
-God. I miss Oliver.

260
00:18:16.471 --> 00:18:17.972
-That's interesting.
-[groans]

261
00:18:18.097 --> 00:18:20.850
Should I tell her that I kissed
Bruno Garcia in fifth grade?

262
00:18:20.934 --> 00:18:24.187
-I kissed that guy a couple times.
-Do whatever you want. Nobody cares.

263
00:18:24.270 --> 00:18:26.397
-I care. I care a lot.
-[groaning]

264
00:18:26.481 --> 00:18:29.692
-We connected in a lot of ways.
-Okay. ew.

265
00:18:29.776 --> 00:18:33.196
I want her to feel like
she can communicate with me.

266
00:18:33.279 --> 00:18:36.074
I feel. generally. pretty good
receiving feedback. You know that.

267
00:18:36.658 --> 00:18:39.035
And so. it's like. if I've done something

268
00:18:39.118 --> 00:18:40.870
-that's made her pull away…
-[yelps]

269
00:18:40.954 --> 00:18:42.622
…I wanna know. so I can--

270
00:18:42.705 --> 00:18:45.375
Okay. Rory. Rory. I'm gonna scream.
Can we please switch?

271
00:18:45.458 --> 00:18:48.253
-Dude. for sure.
-Oh. my God! Oh. my fucking God!

272
00:18:48.336 --> 00:18:49.504
-I'm sorry.
-[groans]

273
00:18:53.132 --> 00:18:54.676
All right. You want me to go deep?

274
00:18:54.759 --> 00:18:57.929
Yeah. you can go deep. 'cause I carry
a lot of tension in my glutes.

275
00:18:58.012 --> 00:19:00.598
Listen. man. it's never gonna work out
between them.

276
00:19:01.266 --> 00:19:06.145
I mean. Annie is not the Canadian bacon.
crunchy granola girl next door.

277
00:19:06.229 --> 00:19:07.146
She's cosplaying.

278
00:19:07.230 --> 00:19:09.190
-Right.
-When she gets back to the city.

279
00:19:09.274 --> 00:19:11.568
and realizes she's been dicking around
all summer

280
00:19:11.651 --> 00:19:15.697
instead of learning a new language
or solving the Pythagorean theorem.

281
00:19:15.780 --> 00:19:19.284
she's gonna freak out
and forget all about Ellis.

282
00:19:20.535 --> 00:19:22.453
You're endgame. sweetie.

283
00:19:29.294 --> 00:19:30.712
-Oh. my God! [screams]
-Whoa!

284
00:19:33.506 --> 00:19:34.716
Ramona [hesitating] Lee…

285
00:19:34.799 --> 00:19:36.885
-Lee.
-Lee. Ramona Lee Campbell!

286
00:19:37.719 --> 00:19:40.054
-You can never do that again. Ever.
-I'm sorry.

287
00:19:40.138 --> 00:19:41.890
No. I was worried sick about you.

288
00:19:41.973 --> 00:19:44.183
-We were all worried sick.
-I know. I'm sorry.

289
00:19:44.267 --> 00:19:46.352
-I'm sorry.
-I'm so sorry. because I was…

290
00:19:46.436 --> 00:19:49.063
-I should've told you about Joe. but I--
-[shushes] Stop. No.

291
00:19:49.147 --> 00:19:50.732
It's completely his fault.

292
00:19:51.316 --> 00:19:54.903
It's. like. actually insane.
when you think about it.

293
00:20:01.326 --> 00:20:03.202
I went to Barrie
to talk to Gordon's lawyer.

294
00:20:05.204 --> 00:20:06.497
-Okay.
-Yeah.

295
00:20:07.790 --> 00:20:12.837
I can get Joe to sign some paperwork
to give up the guardianship or whatever.

296
00:20:14.672 --> 00:20:20.303
Just. like. that way I can move on
and do whatever I want.

297
00:20:20.386 --> 00:20:22.722
Like. I don't know.

298
00:20:24.432 --> 00:20:25.600
live on my own…

299
00:20:26.893 --> 00:20:29.562
or marry Oona and get a cat

300
00:20:30.730 --> 00:20:34.484
and open a butterfly sanctuary
and live happily ever after.

301
00:20:35.693 --> 00:20:38.947
[Annie] Okay.
I wanna unpack all of that. but…

302
00:20:40.406 --> 00:20:43.868
Are you sure that that's what you want?
For Joe to not be involved at all?

303
00:20:44.661 --> 00:20:45.495
Yeah.

304
00:20:46.663 --> 00:20:48.623
Yeah. No. Gordon was my dad.

305
00:20:49.958 --> 00:20:53.544
Fuck all this swooping-in-now shit.
I can take care of myself.

306
00:20:55.505 --> 00:20:57.715
Well. I will support
whatever you wanna do here.

307
00:20:58.716 --> 00:21:00.593
-Thank you.
-Yeah. of course.

308
00:21:02.804 --> 00:21:03.972
Who brought you back?

309
00:21:05.640 --> 00:21:06.474
Oona.

310
00:21:07.725 --> 00:21:10.561
Your eyes literally started sparkling
when you said that.

311
00:21:10.645 --> 00:21:16.776
-[both laugh]
-Is it. like. love love?

312
00:21:19.779 --> 00:21:21.531
Yeah. Yeah.

313
00:21:21.614 --> 00:21:23.992
How do you know that? How does that…

314
00:21:24.075 --> 00:21:27.578
-What does that feel like?
-[chuckles]

315
00:21:33.459 --> 00:21:35.169
Have you ever gone fishing in the rain?

316
00:21:37.672 --> 00:21:39.215
No. Sorry. Of course not.

317
00:21:40.883 --> 00:21:42.218
Um… [chuckles]

318
00:21:48.182 --> 00:21:49.392
You know that feeling when…

319
00:21:49.892 --> 00:21:53.062
when someone jumps out and scares you.
and you almost piss your pants.

320
00:21:53.146 --> 00:21:57.358
and you think your heart's gonna explode.
it's pounding so fast?

321
00:21:58.067 --> 00:22:01.070
And five seconds later. you're fine.

322
00:22:02.196 --> 00:22:03.489
But you also feel like…

323
00:22:05.158 --> 00:22:06.868
you've never felt more alive.

324
00:22:09.287 --> 00:22:10.371
It's kinda like that.

325
00:22:24.844 --> 00:22:27.513
Wow. No days off. huh?

326
00:22:28.097 --> 00:22:29.098
[scoffs]

327
00:22:31.726 --> 00:22:34.687
Like. how… How are we related?

328
00:22:35.271 --> 00:22:38.149
I'm so much cooler than you.
It just doesn't make any sense.

329
00:22:38.232 --> 00:22:39.275
Right.

330
00:22:39.358 --> 00:22:40.735
-Yeah. Of course you are.
-Yeah.

331
00:22:40.818 --> 00:22:43.029
-I'll give it to you.
-Thanks.

332
00:22:47.200 --> 00:22:48.201
No offense. but…

333
00:22:49.410 --> 00:22:50.787
Joe isn't my dad.

334
00:22:51.871 --> 00:22:53.831
Like. he just… He just isn't.

335
00:22:56.375 --> 00:22:57.960
You can be my half-brother. though.

336
00:23:00.630 --> 00:23:01.464
I'll allow it.

337
00:23:01.547 --> 00:23:04.509
[chuckles] Let me think about that one.

338
00:23:04.592 --> 00:23:06.344
-You have to think?
-I'll think about it.

339
00:23:06.427 --> 00:23:08.554
Wow. Ouch. man.

340
00:23:09.263 --> 00:23:10.389
Knife to the heart.

341
00:23:12.683 --> 00:23:18.439
You know. the only weird thing now is.
like. I just found out I have siblings.

342
00:23:18.523 --> 00:23:22.568
and now my half-brother
and my sister are. like…

343
00:23:22.652 --> 00:23:23.611
All right.

344
00:23:23.694 --> 00:23:26.823
-Bow chick-a wow-wow.
-All right. This is when we go.

345
00:23:26.906 --> 00:23:28.616
-Go? What do you mean?
-We're going.

346
00:23:28.699 --> 00:23:30.743
Yeah. we're going.
We're leaving on this boat.

347
00:23:30.827 --> 00:23:31.661
This one?

348
00:23:31.744 --> 00:23:33.371
-[Ramona] Yeah.
-No. we're not.

349
00:23:33.454 --> 00:23:36.165
-[Ramona] Yes. we are.
-No. Get your feet off the seats.

350
00:23:36.249 --> 00:23:37.875
-Jesus.
-You get in here. Get in!

351
00:23:37.959 --> 00:23:40.628
[Ellis] This is the Gallaghers' boat.
Remember the Gallaghers?

352
00:23:40.711 --> 00:23:42.630
-Remember Tom?
-I don't care. This is nice.

353
00:23:42.713 --> 00:23:45.383
[Ellis] Get your freaking feet
off the freaking seats.

354
00:23:45.466 --> 00:23:47.426
-Jesus.
-This is nice. Wait. I wanna…

355
00:23:47.927 --> 00:23:49.428
This is nice!

356
00:23:49.512 --> 00:23:52.890
-[Ellis] I can't even drive this boat.
-Yeah. you can. The key is right there.

357
00:23:53.516 --> 00:23:56.727
["Moonlight Sonata III Presto Agitato"
playing on piano]

358
00:23:59.313 --> 00:24:00.148
[Annie] Dad?

359
00:24:47.737 --> 00:24:48.738
[sighs softly]

360
00:24:49.989 --> 00:24:53.117
-Wow. Oh. sorry.
-No. Shit!

361
00:24:53.201 --> 00:24:54.702
Whoa…

362
00:24:54.785 --> 00:24:57.330
Sorry. I was just looking
for my dad. Uh…

363
00:24:59.040 --> 00:25:00.082
That… I…

364
00:25:00.666 --> 00:25:02.210
I thought you couldn't really play.

365
00:25:03.628 --> 00:25:05.087
I can't. That's not…

366
00:25:05.171 --> 00:25:07.048
-I wasn't playing. Yeah.
-Really? 'Cause…

367
00:25:07.924 --> 00:25:09.050
That was… I was just…

368
00:25:10.218 --> 00:25:11.260
playing…

369
00:25:12.178 --> 00:25:13.346
Uh…

370
00:25:13.429 --> 00:25:15.973
Well. that was really. really beautiful.

371
00:25:16.599 --> 00:25:18.017
-Thanks.
-Is my dad here?

372
00:25:19.101 --> 00:25:23.439
He… I think my mom took him out
on the boat. but they'll be back soon.

373
00:25:23.522 --> 00:25:24.815
Okay. Thank you.

374
00:25:25.358 --> 00:25:26.192
That's okay.

375
00:25:26.275 --> 00:25:28.736
You wanna wait? We can have a little…

376
00:25:29.820 --> 00:25:31.280
-Can have a…
-[chuckles]

377
00:25:32.156 --> 00:25:34.075
I only smoke weed when I can't sleep.

378
00:25:34.742 --> 00:25:36.661
Makes me feel like I'm on the news.

379
00:25:36.744 --> 00:25:37.662
-Okay.
-Yeah.

380
00:25:37.745 --> 00:25:38.913
Or when I…

381
00:25:39.538 --> 00:25:41.832
When I don't really know
what to do with my hands.

382
00:25:46.963 --> 00:25:47.964
When do you leave?

383
00:25:49.340 --> 00:25:51.676
-Tomorrow.
-Thank you. Wow.

384
00:25:51.759 --> 00:25:52.593
Yeah.

385
00:25:53.261 --> 00:25:57.306
I don't start for. like. a couple weeks.

386
00:25:57.390 --> 00:26:00.351
but they make you move in
to do all the dorm stuff.

387
00:26:01.185 --> 00:26:03.938
Right. The dorm stuff.

388
00:26:04.522 --> 00:26:05.523
-Yeah.
-[chuckles]

389
00:26:08.859 --> 00:26:11.028
Um…

390
00:26:11.112 --> 00:26:12.947
You can tell me if this is. like.

391
00:26:14.490 --> 00:26:16.742
way too forward of a move. okay?

392
00:26:16.826 --> 00:26:20.371
But. um. my dad's best friend
from high school

393
00:26:20.454 --> 00:26:22.999
is on the board at Wharton.

394
00:26:24.834 --> 00:26:27.086
Yeah. Finally got my dad on the phone.

395
00:26:27.753 --> 00:26:28.921
I'm talking to him.

396
00:26:29.005 --> 00:26:32.967
and he said he would introduce
the two of you.

397
00:26:34.010 --> 00:26:36.721
-to talk about the admissions process.
-Shit. Wow.

398
00:26:36.804 --> 00:26:39.598
Or even. like.
he'd probably write you a rec.

399
00:26:39.682 --> 00:26:42.810
Or set you up in the best possible way
for when you apply.

400
00:26:42.893 --> 00:26:45.062
And I don't want you to feel. like…

401
00:26:46.272 --> 00:26:49.066
'Cause my dad helped him with his son.
He got him. like.

402
00:26:49.608 --> 00:26:52.278
this job at his dream law firm in D.C..
so he owes him one.

403
00:26:53.446 --> 00:26:56.407
Like. um…. Yeah.

404
00:27:07.084 --> 00:27:08.669
You know. I may stay here. actually.

405
00:27:10.463 --> 00:27:11.422
And do what?

406
00:27:12.757 --> 00:27:14.216
And live.

407
00:27:17.887 --> 00:27:19.722
But nobody lives here.

408
00:27:21.057 --> 00:27:21.932
People live here.

409
00:27:22.016 --> 00:27:24.477
No. I know people… I know.

410
00:27:28.189 --> 00:27:29.190
Wait. for real?

411
00:27:35.404 --> 00:27:36.405
Is this about Ellis?

412
00:27:39.992 --> 00:27:41.160
[sighing]

413
00:27:41.243 --> 00:27:42.536
Sorry. I'm…

414
00:27:42.620 --> 00:27:44.914
-No…
-Nah. I shouldn't have said…

415
00:27:44.997 --> 00:27:47.166
You're good. you're good. Um…

416
00:27:47.249 --> 00:27:48.876
I don't know how to…

417
00:27:50.419 --> 00:27:54.090
-I have just a lot going on at the moment.
-Yeah. I know.

418
00:27:54.173 --> 00:27:56.008
No. there's just… I'm in a bit of a…

419
00:27:57.635 --> 00:27:59.595
cloud. Um…

420
00:28:19.156 --> 00:28:20.408
[shop bell jingles]

421
00:28:32.503 --> 00:28:33.587
Hi.

422
00:28:37.550 --> 00:28:38.551
[sighs]

423
00:28:40.928 --> 00:28:41.762
Well…

424
00:28:42.763 --> 00:28:45.891
Look. Ramona.
I know that you are angry with me. I just…

425
00:28:45.975 --> 00:28:49.103
I wanted to give you some space
for a second. you know?

426
00:28:50.980 --> 00:28:53.190
Giving space seems
to really be your move. eh?

427
00:28:56.610 --> 00:28:58.904
I wanted to respect what Gordon wanted.

428
00:28:58.988 --> 00:29:01.073
He had just lost his daughter.

429
00:29:01.157 --> 00:29:03.784
and you were the closest thing
he had to her.

430
00:29:03.868 --> 00:29:06.787
And he's an incredible father. I knew…

431
00:29:08.372 --> 00:29:11.417
-I knew he'd give you the best life.
-And what if she didn't die?

432
00:29:11.500 --> 00:29:13.127
What were you gonna do then?

433
00:29:16.964 --> 00:29:20.926
The plan was that I was gonna leave Kate.
and your mom would leave Steven.

434
00:29:21.010 --> 00:29:22.511
and we were gonna…

435
00:29:23.596 --> 00:29:26.307
We were gonna raise you
all here. together.

436
00:29:26.390 --> 00:29:28.476
Kate and Steven
would just go along with that?

437
00:29:29.435 --> 00:29:31.896
So instead.
you and Gordon decided to just

438
00:29:31.979 --> 00:29:34.690
keep us apart for our entire lives.

439
00:29:35.608 --> 00:29:37.776
-Why?
-Ramona. it was so complicated.

440
00:29:37.860 --> 00:29:40.196
and we were a mess. you know?

441
00:29:41.113 --> 00:29:46.368
The one person that we needed to have
this conversation with wasn't here.

442
00:29:48.287 --> 00:29:50.206
And Steven. he had his wants.

443
00:29:50.289 --> 00:29:53.918
Gordon didn't want you to carry the burden
of what had happened to your mom.

444
00:29:54.001 --> 00:29:59.131
And we just. at least at first.
thought this would make everyone happier.

445
00:30:00.549 --> 00:30:01.383
But then.

446
00:30:02.927 --> 00:30:06.222
you know. when the shock of it all
wore off with time…

447
00:30:08.933 --> 00:30:10.601
I don't know. It…

448
00:30:11.602 --> 00:30:12.978
It was killing me.

449
00:30:14.563 --> 00:30:17.483
It was killing me. Just every single day.

450
00:30:17.566 --> 00:30:20.152
I felt like I was dying just a little bit

451
00:30:20.236 --> 00:30:23.572
because I knew this isn't
what your mom would've wanted.

452
00:30:24.448 --> 00:30:25.741
And Gordon knew it too.

453
00:30:26.492 --> 00:30:31.080
And so he tried to reconnect you guys.
I mean. he really did.

454
00:30:34.250 --> 00:30:40.130
If Gordon… If Gordon had ever decided
to sell the cottage for some reason.

455
00:30:40.214 --> 00:30:44.260
or if we never came to Muskoka. would you…

456
00:30:45.052 --> 00:30:46.512
Would you have tried to find me?

457
00:30:46.595 --> 00:30:48.514
Of course.

458
00:30:49.014 --> 00:30:50.641
Are you kidding? Of course.

459
00:30:51.976 --> 00:30:56.730
For so long. I have thought about
this moment and this conversation.

460
00:30:57.314 --> 00:31:00.651
Always struggled trying to find the words
to be able to explain it.

461
00:31:01.277 --> 00:31:06.490
But the one thing I do know is
I have always felt like I was your dad.

462
00:31:09.243 --> 00:31:10.494
Yeah. but you aren't.

463
00:31:12.121 --> 00:31:13.038
[sniffles]

464
00:31:13.622 --> 00:31:14.873
Gordon was my dad.

465
00:31:17.543 --> 00:31:19.628
Yeah. and a damn good one.

466
00:31:21.338 --> 00:31:22.172
Yeah.

467
00:31:27.511 --> 00:31:28.721
I need you to sign this.

468
00:31:31.932 --> 00:31:32.766
What is it?

469
00:31:34.643 --> 00:31:36.520
I don't want you to be my guardian.

470
00:31:39.857 --> 00:31:43.569
Look. Ramona. I know you don't want anyone
breathing down your neck.

471
00:31:44.320 --> 00:31:46.405
Just let me do this for you.

472
00:31:46.488 --> 00:31:48.616
I can take care of all this stuff.

473
00:31:48.699 --> 00:31:50.909
make sure you get the check
from Gordon's estate.

474
00:31:50.993 --> 00:31:54.246
-You don't even have to see or talk to me.
-No. I don't want that.

475
00:31:59.668 --> 00:32:00.669
I can't.

476
00:32:00.753 --> 00:32:02.338
-[scoffing] Excuse me?
-I can't.

477
00:32:03.714 --> 00:32:05.716
See. if I sign this. I am doubling down

478
00:32:05.799 --> 00:32:07.926
on the biggest mistake
I ever made in my life.

479
00:32:08.010 --> 00:32:11.138
And. Ramona. I can fix this.
Let me fix this.

480
00:32:11.221 --> 00:32:14.266
-I don't want you to fix anything!
-Look. I get it.

481
00:32:14.975 --> 00:32:18.771
You hate me right now. all right?
But the answer is no.

482
00:32:19.521 --> 00:32:22.107
Gordon appointed me your guardian.

483
00:32:22.191 --> 00:32:23.817
That is what he wanted.

484
00:32:23.901 --> 00:32:25.069
Yeah. well. he's not here.

485
00:32:25.152 --> 00:32:27.279
So how can you say
that's really what he wanted?

486
00:32:28.656 --> 00:32:30.032
Maybe you were the only choice.

487
00:32:30.115 --> 00:32:32.201
Then you tell me.
What do you think he wanted?

488
00:32:32.284 --> 00:32:36.664
I don't know. but if you expect any
type of relationship to come from this.

489
00:32:37.581 --> 00:32:40.417
trust it will only be biological.

490
00:32:41.585 --> 00:32:46.340
Because if you think. even for a second.
that I'm forgiving you. ever.

491
00:32:47.758 --> 00:32:48.842
you are delusional.

492
00:32:55.432 --> 00:32:57.142
-[door closes]
-[sighs]

493
00:32:58.060 --> 00:33:01.063
["Begging For Rain" playing]

494
00:33:17.371 --> 00:33:18.205
I'm right here.

495
00:33:42.271 --> 00:33:46.233
"Dear Ramona. it feels strange
to write you this letter

496
00:33:46.316 --> 00:33:48.485
after you just beat me in Scrabble."

497
00:33:49.570 --> 00:33:55.534
"The 'Q' on the triple-letter score
was rather brutal. but all is forgiven."

498
00:33:56.368 --> 00:34:00.497
"I wanted… No. needed to tell you
how proud I am of you."

499
00:34:02.249 --> 00:34:03.083
"You amaze me."

500
00:34:04.543 --> 00:34:05.919
"You amaze me every day."

501
00:34:06.545 --> 00:34:10.048
"Your stubbornness. your sense of humor.
your strength."

502
00:34:10.132 --> 00:34:15.512
"You've always been exactly who you are.
and I love that person dearly."

503
00:34:17.097 --> 00:34:19.808
"Thank you for giving me
the honor of raising you."

504
00:34:22.186 --> 00:34:28.484
"It gave me a second chance at having
a daughter after we lost your mom."

505
00:34:31.278 --> 00:34:34.156
[sobs] "I wish the two of you
could've spent more time together."

506
00:34:35.783 --> 00:34:38.035
"I know you would've
made each other laugh."

507
00:34:40.245 --> 00:34:42.623
"I'm sorry there were things
I didn't tell you."

508
00:34:45.501 --> 00:34:47.586
[sniffing] "Hindsight is 20-20.

509
00:34:49.546 --> 00:34:53.675
but I wanted you to know. at the time.
this felt like the right decision."

510
00:34:54.176 --> 00:34:55.594
"Maybe the only decision."

511
00:34:57.095 --> 00:35:02.518
"But now I know I was very wrong.
and I'm incredibly sorry. my dear."

512
00:35:04.228 --> 00:35:05.521
"But you are not alone."

513
00:35:06.188 --> 00:35:10.609
"You have a family.
and I hope you've found each other

514
00:35:11.109 --> 00:35:14.905
and. together. will make up
for lost time."

515
00:35:16.323 --> 00:35:21.286
"I know they will cherish you
as much as I have cherished you."

516
00:35:24.206 --> 00:35:25.374
"Love always.

517
00:35:27.251 --> 00:35:28.377
Gordon."

518
00:35:32.756 --> 00:35:34.132
[sobbing]

519
00:36:03.579 --> 00:36:06.707
[Annie] <i>Ramona. that's so intense.</i>
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

520
00:36:06.790 --> 00:36:08.750
[Ramona] <i>Yeah. no. it's okay. actually.</i>

521
00:36:09.334 --> 00:36:11.086
I'm really glad I read it.

522
00:36:12.838 --> 00:36:15.966
I guess we'll see about. you know.
what'll happen with Joe.

523
00:36:16.049 --> 00:36:16.884
Yeah.

524
00:36:18.844 --> 00:36:22.347
Well. I'm here for you for all of it.

525
00:36:22.431 --> 00:36:24.099
Any… Anything you need.

526
00:36:26.894 --> 00:36:29.187
You know. I'm really. really proud of you.

527
00:36:33.150 --> 00:36:34.026
I am.

528
00:36:39.781 --> 00:36:41.909
How are you feeling about
going back to New York?

529
00:36:43.285 --> 00:36:45.329
What's the latest with your dad?

530
00:36:45.412 --> 00:36:46.580
Um…

531
00:36:46.663 --> 00:36:49.249
You know what? I honestly don't even know.

532
00:36:49.750 --> 00:36:52.210
I went to go see him this morning.
and he was not there.

533
00:36:52.294 --> 00:36:54.254
-Oh.
-Yeah. so…

534
00:36:54.796 --> 00:36:56.632
Aside from that. I'm obviously devastated.

535
00:36:57.382 --> 00:37:00.302
I'd rather die than leave Sterling Point
and you and…

536
00:37:01.219 --> 00:37:02.638
-[sighs] You know…
-And?

537
00:37:04.306 --> 00:37:07.434
-No. nothing. I didn't say anything.
-Annie…

538
00:37:08.518 --> 00:37:09.353
What?

539
00:37:10.437 --> 00:37:13.190
-I'm brushing… I'm in the middle--
-You were about to say Ellis.

540
00:37:13.273 --> 00:37:14.358
-No.
-Yeah. you were.

541
00:37:14.983 --> 00:37:16.526
-No. I wasn't.
-Yeah. you were.

542
00:37:17.319 --> 00:37:19.071
-No. I wasn't.
-What?

543
00:37:22.783 --> 00:37:23.825
We did kiss.

544
00:37:23.909 --> 00:37:25.160
-[gasps]
-I know.

545
00:37:25.243 --> 00:37:26.411
-Shut up.
-In the closet.

546
00:37:26.495 --> 00:37:27.955
-In the--
-On the floor.

547
00:37:28.830 --> 00:37:31.291
-And he dragged me on the floor.
-Wait.

548
00:37:31.375 --> 00:37:34.461
-In a really good way.
-Yeah. that's a great place for a kiss.

549
00:37:34.544 --> 00:37:36.046
Dragged. in a nice way.

550
00:37:36.129 --> 00:37:38.131
It was a perfect place for a kiss.

551
00:37:38.674 --> 00:37:41.969
Wait. I'm so glad I'm telling you this.
It was the perfect place for a kiss.

552
00:37:42.678 --> 00:37:44.972
and it was a perfect kiss.

553
00:37:45.055 --> 00:37:46.139
-Fuck.
-Like. a perfect--

554
00:37:46.223 --> 00:37:48.600
No shit. You guys slow-burned
the shit out of it.

555
00:37:48.684 --> 00:37:50.560
-Yeah. we did. Yeah.
-It took you forever…

556
00:37:50.644 --> 00:37:51.770
-Okay. turn.
-Okay.

557
00:37:51.853 --> 00:37:56.316
But now I'm like. what do people do?

558
00:37:56.400 --> 00:37:58.110
Like. how do people do this?

559
00:37:58.902 --> 00:38:01.405
-Do what? What do you mean?
-Like. be with someone.

560
00:38:01.488 --> 00:38:03.782
Not… We're obviously
not in a relationship.

561
00:38:03.865 --> 00:38:05.492
-Right.
-But it's just occurring to me

562
00:38:05.575 --> 00:38:11.581
that I literally have no idea what to do
or how to be in this context.

563
00:38:11.665 --> 00:38:15.043
Know what I mean? I feel like
I know myself pretty well in other ways.

564
00:38:15.127 --> 00:38:18.088
I'd like to think that. But with this.
I'm like. "Oh. I'm a baby."

565
00:38:18.171 --> 00:38:19.631
I'm a newborn baby. I'm an idiot.

566
00:38:19.715 --> 00:38:22.009
-You're not. Don't say that.
-It's not a bad thing.

567
00:38:22.092 --> 00:38:24.094
-It's just. when we were at camp…
-Yeah.

568
00:38:24.177 --> 00:38:27.556
…I literally shared the deepest pits
of my brain with him.

569
00:38:27.639 --> 00:38:30.017
-Yeah?
-Sorry. I'm just gonna get…

570
00:38:30.726 --> 00:38:32.811
There. I shared the deepest pits
of my brain.

571
00:38:32.894 --> 00:38:34.730
-Okay.
-The ugliest. worst parts.

572
00:38:34.813 --> 00:38:37.441
I shared them at him. okay? At him.

573
00:38:37.524 --> 00:38:42.487
Now I just am supposed to be
completely vulnerable with this person?

574
00:38:42.571 --> 00:38:43.572
Like…

575
00:38:43.655 --> 00:38:44.906
-Yeah.
-Do you want a braid?

576
00:38:44.990 --> 00:38:46.033
Yeah. sure.

577
00:38:46.116 --> 00:38:47.909
-And this is the feeling.
-What?

578
00:38:47.993 --> 00:38:49.786
This is the feeling everyone talks about.

579
00:38:49.870 --> 00:38:52.873
the feeling that makes
the literal world spin around.

580
00:38:52.956 --> 00:38:55.584
Oh. my God!
Make me stop talking about this.

581
00:38:55.667 --> 00:38:58.045
I feel like this is torture for you.

582
00:38:58.128 --> 00:38:59.463
No. it's not.

583
00:38:59.546 --> 00:39:01.006
I mean. yeah. I…

584
00:39:02.215 --> 00:39:05.802
I get it. It's definitely fucked
to feel like

585
00:39:05.886 --> 00:39:08.388
someone is holding your heart
outside of your body.

586
00:39:08.472 --> 00:39:10.891
and they could just smash it at any…

587
00:39:11.683 --> 00:39:14.102
at any time for any reason and. like…

588
00:39:15.103 --> 00:39:17.064
Yeah. Yeah. I get it.

589
00:39:17.147 --> 00:39:18.315
Yeah.

590
00:39:18.398 --> 00:39:19.274
Yeah.

591
00:39:19.357 --> 00:39:21.693
Like. how do you do that?
How do I do that?

592
00:39:22.360 --> 00:39:24.988
If you really do wanna keep talking to him
after you leave.

593
00:39:25.072 --> 00:39:26.698
you gotta get him Internet.

594
00:39:26.782 --> 00:39:29.159
It's like. this is what
I'm supposed to be doing.

595
00:39:29.993 --> 00:39:32.204
-Making out with a hot guy in a closet.
-Mmm!

596
00:39:32.287 --> 00:39:33.622
And finding myself.

597
00:39:33.705 --> 00:39:36.583
-Yeah.
-Yeah. and not dating a guy in the closet

598
00:39:36.666 --> 00:39:40.879
and organizing my dad's socks
so he doesn't mix them up.

599
00:39:40.962 --> 00:39:41.797
Like. can…

600
00:39:42.255 --> 00:39:44.841
[grunting] Let me live!
You know what I mean?

601
00:39:46.009 --> 00:39:48.637
Wait. why do you check
your dad's socks for him?

602
00:39:48.720 --> 00:39:51.681
'Cause he's colorblind. so he mixes up
navy blue and black.

603
00:39:54.601 --> 00:39:57.312
Make sure you brush your tongue.
You always forget.

604
00:40:08.198 --> 00:40:10.742
-Hey. Can I use your laptop for a sec?
-Hey.

605
00:40:10.826 --> 00:40:14.246
I'm in the middle of an order.
I'm trying to get some more tinned fish.

606
00:40:14.329 --> 00:40:16.581
A brand I like is about to drop
new smoked mackerel…

607
00:40:16.665 --> 00:40:18.166
-Okay.
-…so I wanna be-- Awesome.

608
00:40:18.250 --> 00:40:20.418
Please take care of my electronics.
thank you.

609
00:40:23.922 --> 00:40:27.425
Are you taking a summer school
biology class I don't know about?

610
00:40:27.509 --> 00:40:29.136
What's going on?

611
00:40:35.809 --> 00:40:37.477
Ramona. what's going on? Are you okay?

612
00:40:39.563 --> 00:40:40.397
Yeah. I'm fine.

613
00:40:40.480 --> 00:40:42.399
You know how I feel
about that word from you.

614
00:40:42.482 --> 00:40:43.775
-I'm fine.
-Okay.

615
00:40:44.526 --> 00:40:45.485
[inhales]

616
00:40:45.569 --> 00:40:46.611
Can I speak freely?

617
00:40:47.362 --> 00:40:48.238
Mmm-hmm.

618
00:40:48.321 --> 00:40:52.576
I think that you are really.
really good at hiding.

619
00:40:53.160 --> 00:40:56.329
Scarily good at it. Nobody could ever
find you when we played sardines.

620
00:40:56.413 --> 00:40:59.124
Okay. Do you ever
stop talking about tinned fish?

621
00:40:59.207 --> 00:41:00.333
We're having a moment.

622
00:41:01.001 --> 00:41:01.877
Sorry.

623
00:41:03.461 --> 00:41:05.589
I don't really know what the situation is.

624
00:41:06.715 --> 00:41:10.302
but I can tell that it's important.
and I can tell that it's real.

625
00:41:10.927 --> 00:41:15.223
so. what if. instead of hiding from it
this time. what if you just…

626
00:41:16.766 --> 00:41:18.268
went ahead and just faced it?

627
00:41:21.104 --> 00:41:21.938
Yeah. but…

628
00:41:24.399 --> 00:41:25.817
-I don't know if I can.
-You can.

629
00:41:27.485 --> 00:41:28.987
I've seen it. Ramona. You can.

630
00:41:30.989 --> 00:41:32.824
You're one of the strongest people I know.

631
00:41:36.703 --> 00:41:38.663
And you never have to
go through things alone.

632
00:41:41.249 --> 00:41:43.293
Why are you the best? It's stupid.

633
00:41:43.376 --> 00:41:45.128
I don't know. [chuckling]

634
00:41:45.212 --> 00:41:47.589
Maybe she's born with it.
maybe it's mackerel.

635
00:41:47.672 --> 00:41:49.216
-[laughs]
-Yeah. [chuckles]

636
00:41:49.299 --> 00:41:51.593
I won't even apologize for that.
It was pretty good.

637
00:41:51.676 --> 00:41:53.261
-Yeah.
-Incredible. actually.

638
00:41:53.345 --> 00:41:54.179
Mmm.

639
00:41:55.639 --> 00:41:56.556
You're gonna be okay.

640
00:41:57.307 --> 00:41:59.559
["Hero" playing]

641
00:42:07.067 --> 00:42:09.444
Oh. Hey. Ramona. Hi.

642
00:42:10.028 --> 00:42:11.196
Hey.

643
00:42:11.279 --> 00:42:14.824
Um. I'm really happy
you got home safe and sound.

644
00:42:16.076 --> 00:42:17.118
Cool.

645
00:42:17.202 --> 00:42:21.998
Well. uh. I was gonna head out. actually.
and go see if I could talk to Annie.

646
00:42:22.082 --> 00:42:23.583
I. just… I wanna talk to you.

647
00:42:25.293 --> 00:42:27.254
Okay. sure. What's up?

648
00:42:28.505 --> 00:42:29.798
I need you to spit in a tube.

649
00:42:31.216 --> 00:42:34.135
[chuckles] Okay. Um. can I ask why?

650
00:42:34.219 --> 00:42:35.470
Because…

651
00:42:36.805 --> 00:42:38.390
I think you might be my dad.

652
00:42:39.305 --> 00:43:39.327
